From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:25:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] ARM: dts: qcom: add separate Madai CPU qualification
 target

Retain the current ordinary board charging, USB, NFC and other device
definitions. Add only the L2/S2 CPU foundation and complete eight-byte
CPU calibration row. Its ordinary four CPU rates and absent CPR consumer
remain unchanged. A separate explicit qualification target describes all
fourteen canonical rates and their matching domain links.

The other eighteen platform DTBs are byte-identical to the prior
qualified frontend; both changed Fx0 targets pass complete schemas. No
image is installed or booted by this source change.

Composite port from Fx0 CPU source
790c9c5407e17ad1d2395c2ec4bdfcfc8dc82826. Original component author and
date retained; the scoped original source history is recorded in the
qualification evidence. Port, current API merges, changelog and
qualification used OpenAI Codex assistance.

